# empty-matches-step-one-character: when every match is empty, the Match
# Search finds one at each position, stepping one Character past each empty
# match it discards. `optional "x"` over "ab" gives an empty match before
# each Character and one at the end, ranges 1..0, 2..1 and 3..2 (spec
# chapter 4, Matches; chapter 8, Running). The matches and ranges are
# pinned. Fuel, allocation and state are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load search

# Six searches of 2 steps each, 12 steps: a kept empty match at 0, 1 and 2,
# each followed by a search from the same position whose empty match is
# discarded, moving the next search one Character on.
> deliver d1 to=search message=go
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg search/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=go clause=1 fuel=29 alloc=733 state=733 end=return
run search/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=go fuel=29 alloc=733
pumped state=idle fuel=29

> vars
vars search hits=[{text: "", range: 1..0, captures: {}, ranges: {}}, {text: "", range: 2..1, captures: {}, ranges: {}}, {text: "", range: 3..2, captures: {}, ranges: {}}]
